<title>USA: Sedgwick Group trades on NYSE.</title>
<headline>Sedgwick Group trades on NYSE.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sedgwick Group Plc, the risk advisory, insurance brokerage and employee benefits consulting firm, began trading on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) on Monday.</p>
<p>Sedgwick, which trades under the symbol &quot;SED,&quot; opened Monday's trading at 10-3/8 and closed 1/4 higher at 10-5/8. Sedgwick security will be an American despository security (ADS), in which one ADS comprises five ordinary shares.</p>
<p>Sedgwick has 548,468,441 shares in issue.</p>
<p>The firm, which has its global headquarters in London and North American headquarters in Memphis, will continue to trade on the London Stock Exchange as well.</p>
